>> title: Soft Pretzels
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, pretzels, snack, boiled, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: Bavarian pretzel, brezel, laugenbrezel
>> pairs-with: cheddar-cheese-sauce
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr
>> step.1: stir, stand 10 min
>> step.2: add and knead 8 min
>> step.3: cover, rise until doubled
>> step.4: divide into eight ropes, twist
>> step.5: dip 30 sec in the soda bath
>> step.6: egg-wash, salt, bake 450°F 14 min

Stir @warm water{1 1/2%cup}(355 mL) with @light brown sugar{2%Tbs}(27 g) and @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), then let stand ~{10%min}.

Add @bread flour{4 1/2%cup}(610 g), @table salt{2%tsp}(12 g), and @melted unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(55 g) to @&(~1)yeast mixture{}, then knead ~{8%min}.

Cover @&(~1)dough{} and rise until doubled, ~{1%hour}.

Divide @&(~1)dough{} into eight ropes and twist into pretzels.

Dip @&(~1)pretzels{} for ~{30%sec} into boiling water with @baking soda{2/3%cup}(150 g).

Brush @&(~1)pretzels{} with @beaten egg{1%large}, sprinkle with @pretzel salt{2%Tbs}, and bake at 450°F for ~{14%min}.
